  "prefLabel": "Phy 305.01 Eligibility Requirements for Initial Licensure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Phy 305.01 Eligibility Requirements for Initial Licensure.\n\n(a) Applicants for initial licensure as physical therapists or physical therapist assistants shall:\n\n(1) Be of good moral character as evidenced by:\n\na. The answers to the questions on the application form described in Phy 304.01(a);\n\nb. Any reports submitted pursuant to the requirements of the application form described in Phy 304.01(b);\n\nc. Any information about the applicant’s licenses or other authorizations to practice physical therapy; and\n\nd. The criminal history record reports required by RSA 328-F:18-a.\n\n(2) If applicable, have met the English language proficiency testing requirement of Phy 306.04;\n\n(3) Have taken and passed the national physical therapy examination for physical therapists or the national physical therapy examination for physical therapist assistants, as applicable; and\n\n(4) Have taken and passed the jurisprudence assessment module as described in Phy 303.04; and\n\n(5) Have met the continuing competency requirements as defined in Phy 302.03.\n\n(b) Pursuant to RSA 332-G:7, the board shall consider military experience applicable to the education of physical therapists or physical therapist assistants when determining whether an applicant meets the educational or experience requirements for licensure.\n\nSource. #9233, eff 8-22-08; ss by #9429, eff 3-19-09; ss by #9869, eff 2-18-11; ss by #10401, eff 8-23-13; ss by #10724, eff 11-22-14; amd by #10933, eff 9-18-15; ss by #12087, eff 1-20-17; ss by #12864, eff 9-10-19; ss by #14563, eff 6-20-26, EXPIRES: 6-20-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/phy300.html"
